Z||000000||Orlando||08-05-99||09:20 PM||||Ok, you guys have been right on in helping me fix most of the problems on my 88 Formula, but I seem to have developed a new one! After correcting a cracked EGR tube problem that caused the engine to idle roughly, I'm starting to hear a couple of wierd noises. I'll try to be as onomatopoetic as possible!<p>#1. I hear a sort of "flit, flit, flit" kind of sound (like air escaping) when accelerating.<p>#2. I also hear a harsh rasp sound when I shift at about 4500 RPM. <p>#3. The tach goes nuts at about 4700 RPM.<p>#4. I hear a metalic "goink" sound when I take corners.<p>What's happening? I fix something then something else breaks. My wife is going to kill me if I have to spend money on some major repairs!<p>I read something once
Z||000001||theogre||08-05-99||10:40 PM||||I'll do this in reverse............<p>4. make sure the sheilds are not hitting the brake rotors. There is just enough play in even new hubs to allow the rear sheilds to hit in a hard turn.<p>3. the tach filter is probably bad.<p>2. is it a stick, or auto tranny? In a stick I'd say the clutch is close to frying. In an auto, you got a large problem.<p>1. hell if I know...... because the intake is on the rear fender, sometimes you here air intake noise. (V6 is great for this, but my 4 does it to.) If the dog bone is bad, or not setup right, you could have someting rubbing if the motor is shifting wrong when you stand on it. 
Z||000002||Patrick||08-05-99||10:40 PM||||<br>Was that last sentence supposed to impress us?  <IMG SRC="http://www.compucheap.com/ubb/smile.gif"> <p>
Z||000003||Patrick||08-05-99||10:41 PM||||<br>I was referring to Orlando's post!  <IMG SRC="http://www.compucheap.com/ubb/smile.gif"> <p>
Z||000004||mwbackus||08-06-99||01:53 AM||||1.  Crack exhaust manifold.. common problem with V6.<p>2.  Insufficient Info..<p>3.  Tach Filter<p>4.  Goink suppressor worn or out of adjustment (just kidding).
Z||000005||DJRice||08-06-99||12:07 PM||||I'll bet it wasn't the Haynes Manual that got read just once!
Z||000006||Orlando||08-06-99||08:34 PM||||Thanks for the advice guys!<br>I took off one of the real wheels to check if the brake shields could be possibly making contact with anything else. I don't think so, but <br>I did notice that there is some rust on the struts and the control arms. Maybe it's time for new ones.<p>The tach filter has been replaced, and when I changed it, the problem seemed to go away for a couple of days, but it came right back.<p>I don't think the clutch is slipping or grabbing funny, I can smoke the tires pretty well without too much effort. The rasp sounds more like massive pinging than a clutch problem. But I could be wrong.<p>I bought a goink suppressor from the Pontiac dealer, and replaced it according to the instructions in the Haynes manual. It still goinks. I called GM and they said that they are aware of the problem, and there is a "silent recall" in effect for the updated goink supressor!<p>I think I may have to "break down" and drop the car off at the dealership for a few days.
Z||000007||mwbackus||08-08-99||10:25 PM||||I got a pretty bad ping problem too, a combination of cheap utah gas, hot climate, and carbon buildup I presume.  I will either move or clean the engine up a bit I guess.  You could try using some premium gas and retarding the timing a bit to see if it helps.  The cracked exhaust manifold is something I would check for still, the "flit, flit" describes this very well. I guess it is possible you got a bad tach filter, but, based on your previous replacement results I would suspect some bad wires/connections.  As far as the goink suppressor goes, I would just remove it and install the new Holly Goink Annihilator system, they say its good for a few extra HP and you get a nice sticker too. :-)
Z||000008||Ozzy||08-08-99||11:52 PM||||Hey guys...<p>Ditto on the Haynes thing. The non shiny surface makes great backup TP!<p>Anyone know of a decent shop manual that might actually describe the stuff on MY year and model??? <p>If possible a special addendum on (you guessed it) goink adjustment and removal!<br>(sorry I couldn't help myself) Hope Orlando gets his problems solved without divorce!<p>Ozzy
Z||000009||DJRice||08-09-99||07:29 AM||||It is surprising that with all the advances in automotive technology, the goink suppressors havent improved all that much.  Goink Suppression Technology (GST) is starting to come to the forefront again, because goinks are becoming widespread and very bothersome.  I agree that the Holley Goink Annhiliator is a very impressive device, but I have the Goinkinator 5000 from Goink Racing Technology.  Not only does it virtually eliminate the goinks, but it also offers an impressive extra 25HP.  Guaranteed!  But wait theres more, (More you say?) Yes, More!  The new Goinkinator comes in 3 new fresh scents.<p>Order now and we'll include the "Goinkinator Fuel Enhancer" and brand new Goinkinator window sticker.  Both of these great products offer a 5HP increase each! <p>But I digress.....
Z||000010||Orlando||08-09-99||05:15 PM||||Thakns for the replies guys! I think I will just take the car into the local Pontiac dealer and let the monkies work on the car. I'm going to start by suggesting that they check for recalls, and look at the exhaust manifolds. I've seen other Fieros with the Holley Goink Annhiliator installed, but it just doesn't look stock. It must be a pain to remove it and the reinstall it for show. You know how those purists are!<p>Hey, anyone care for a free factory subwoofer setup? Just kidding! I have one I yanked of of my dearly departed '86 GT, but I'm too lazy to install it. I guess I'll wait 'till most of the broken stuff gets fixed.<p>
Z||000011||Formula||08-10-99||10:17 AM||||I'll trade you my pro millenium goink crusher with preamplified goink destroying abillities that sits under the holley goink annhilator for your sub!!!!
